  want your explicit go-ahead before touching it.

  [1mConsequence:[0m a 16× longer session lifetime means a stolen or hijacked session token stays valid for 8 hours instead of
  30 minutes, and unattended/shared machines stay logged in for a full workday. Idle-logout is often the control that
  satisfies an auth/compliance requirement, so this can silently break one.

  Two things worth knowing:

  - [38;5;153mserver.js[39m only logs the value — there's no actual expiry enforcement in this repo, so the real impact depends on
    whatever consumes this config downstream.
  - If the goal is "stop logging users out mid-work," a sliding/idle timeout (30 min idle, 8 hour absolute cap) gets
    that without the exposure window. That's a design choice, not a value swap.

  Confirm and I'll make the straight 30 → 480 change as asked.

